Z||000000||danny boy||05-31-2001||10:57 PM|||| I recently aquired 15 acres of property and have finally started making something of it. I don't know the first thing about country living( the neighbor just looked at me funny when I told him I had never been hunting)but Dammit I'm gonna find out!!!<BR> I'm estatic. I have 1 and 1/2 horses and they now have a home that I own!  Mmm...Now I have room for parts cars....||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-31-2001||11:06 PM||||Country livin' is the best!!!  I wouldnt trade it for anything else.  I dont live too far away from anything, but we still have our privacy and the best neighbors in the world.  <BR>Now that you have enough land, you can build a nice big pole barn, with the stalls for your horses, a hay loft if you want and a tack room, a nice corral, and probably still have enough room left over to keep a car or two to work on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You're going to need a 4x4 truck, you know that right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I would have to say the most essential thing we've got here is a nice deck to sit out on in the evenings, and just listen to the silence.  So very peaceful out here, the only sounds are the creatures that chirp and ribbit in the neighbors pond.<P>Hunting is fun too.  I dont know about the seasons where you live, but I firearm deer hunt up here, and that season is in November.  It's pretty cool, being out in our woods (we have 10 acres), where everything is still and peaceful.<P>Ug, I'm getting all mushy here!  I better stop.<P>But anyway, congrats, I think anyone who has an open mind can enjoy living a life other than city life.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||05-31-2001||11:10 PM|||| I was out the there for a while tonight, just sitting on a log(which I had cut with my very first chainsaw) for at least an hour just listening to the stream. Oh, how great it is.||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||05-31-2001||11:39 PM||||You'll love the country!! cept maybe in mid-winter. But just wonderin, that 1/2 horse you own; is it the front half or back half?<BR>If it's the front half, you gotta feed it but if it's the back half,& a female, you can still have it bred but you half to shovel horse poop. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Boy, I got too much time on my hands!!||||reg||12
Z||000004||Phil||05-31-2001||11:53 PM||||Don't forget the thrill of bugs||||reg||1
