Z||000006||Cheever2||06-01-2001||01:51 AM||||Ahh, we rented an old house in the country for a year, when we lived in southwest Ohio.  80 acres.  The house wasn't much good, it should be torn down and rebuilt, but the memories were wonderful.  Nice front porch to sit & look out across the long yard to the road.  Creek running by, with a wooden bridge to walk across.  Barn.  Old outhouse.  Deer in the mornings.  Couldn't see another house in any direction.  Several enormous pine trees.  Had a 100 foot well, and the water was wonderful.  Barely survived a brutal summer and then one of their worst winters, but there were more good times there in one year than I could list here.<BR> ||||reg||6
