Z||000008||turbo86se||06-01-2001||10:52 AM||||Hmmm, this makes me want to get out of the maddness of Myrtle Beach and cruise on down to the family plantation in Georgetown. We've got two houses on the Black River and 500 acres, all along the river. I love going down there, especially at night, real quiet, lots of stars in the sky, sit out on front screen porch or the boat dock with a cold beer. I'd go swimming if it weren't for all the alligators splashing around (you can hear them from the house). I grandfather used to tell me of a 15 foot gator that lived very close to the house in one of the rice fields, that was many years ago, I wander how big he is now?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||06-01-2001||10:58 AM||||one of the things I regret about modern life is that most of our ancestors built their own homes - I think we pay dearly for letting someone else do that for us.<P>  Ive wanted for a long time to get some land out in the country and build my own place - even if its only a cabin.<P>  Congrats on the acquision.||||reg||1
